-- ----- minimum -------------------------------------------------------------

@label "minimum Preimage"
@description "Aggregable.preimageOf instance for `minimum`. Given an output `SetExpr` over the aggregator's output type, return the canonical `$where`-wrapped preimage `{v | minimum(v) ∈ outputSet}`, or `Nothing` when the output set has no closed-form preimage. NOTE (signature-substrate slice 3c-D2): `std:minimum` is now honestly typed `List a -> Maybe a`, so the aggregator's OUTPUT TYPE — and therefore the type `outputSet` must range over — is `Maybe a`, not `a`. `{v | minimum(v) ∈ SeEnum [5]}` is now genuinely EMPTY (`Just 5 ∉ {5}`) and the emitted predicate evaluating false everywhere is CORRECT, not unsound; the meaningful query is `SeEnum [Just 5]`, which the equality arm decides exactly because `eq` is structural. Callers passing a bare-`a` output set get the honest empty set."
@tags "aggregable" "preimage" "minimum"
minimumPreimageOf : (outputSet: SetExpr) -> Maybe SetExpr
minimumPreimageOf outputSet = genericPreimageOf "minimum" outputSet

@native
@label "minimum Image"
@description "Aggregable.imageOf instance for `minimum`. Given an input `SetExpr`, return the aggregator's output image when expressible in closed form. Phase 9 ships a conservative implementation that returns the aggregator's declared outputType (e.g. `Nat` for length/count) — refining with input-set-aware tightening is a future Aggregable enhancement."
@tags "aggregable" "image" "minimum"
